"supply or physical timing. Uninspected PCB revisions and jumpers remain "
"unknown; software fixtures do not qualify a real PCB. MCU physical HIL "
"remains `not_executed`."

msgid "Each MCU family owns `soc.json`, `routes.json`, its private controller state, selected driver sources and explicit CMake targets. Its `configure/` package owns family capabilities, admission, construction and lifecycle emission. Provider tests remain in `tools/configure/tests/providers/<family>/`; shared parsing, typed IR, resource arbitration and bundle transactions remain in `tools/configure/`. Startup, clocks, timebase, memory and power code remain with that family. Reusable IP algorithms live in [drivers](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/drivers/README.md) and are shared only after every wrapper checks the real vendor layout, bits, clocks, IRQ/DMA routes and errata. Similar peripheral names do not establish equivalence."
msgstr "Each MCU family owns `soc.json`, `routes.json`, its private controller state, selected driver sources and explicit CMake targets. Its `configure/` package owns family capabilities, admission, construction and lifecycle emission. Provider tests remain in `tools/configure/tests/providers/<family>/`; shared parsing, typed IR, resource arbitration and bundle transactions remain in `tools/configure/`. Startup, clocks, timebase, memory and power code remain with that family. Reusable IP algorithms live in [drivers](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/drivers/README.md) and are shared only after every wrapper checks the real vendor layout, bits, clocks, IRQ/DMA routes and errata. Similar peripheral names do not establish equivalence."

msgid "`native/drivers/` implements the public I/O contracts as independent host models; it does not establish MCU timing or electrical behavior. `common/uart_control.h` is a cross-vendor SoC collaboration contract; STM32 identity access belongs in `stm32/common/stm32_identity.h`. Neither is a reusable peripheral algorithm."
msgstr "`native/drivers/` implements the public I/O contracts as independent host models; it does not establish MCU timing or electrical behavior. `common/uart_control.h` is a cross-vendor SoC collaboration contract; STM32 identity access belongs in `stm32/common/stm32_identity.h`. Neither is a reusable peripheral algorithm."

