msgid "The I2C V1 engine is shared by STM32F407, GD32F470, STM32F103 and GD32F303. The first pair retains its reviewed 100 kHz profile. The 8 MHz low-end pair uses nominal 80 kHz, priority-zero non-kernel IRQs and no I2C DMA. ES096 2.8.1/2.8.5 and GD32F30x limitations 2.8.1 require these narrower choices. The F4 stream-DMA layout is never reused for a fixed-channel controller. Captured wake publishers join before stop returns borrowed notification storage; a refused vector withdrawal retains the initialized owner for explicit retry. Each SoC wrapper verifies its actual SDK register offsets and bit definitions, supplies exact clock, DMA/IRQ and visible-memory facts, and binds the selected static state. Matching register names cannot establish another chip's routing, pin wiring, clock rate or errata policy."
msgstr "The I2C V1 engine is shared by STM32F407, GD32F470, STM32F103 and GD32F303. The first pair retains its reviewed 100 kHz profile. The 8 MHz low-end pair uses nominal 80 kHz, priority-zero non-kernel IRQs and no I2C DMA. ES096 2.8.1/2.8.5 and GD32F30x limitations 2.8.1 require these narrower choices. The F4 stream-DMA layout is never reused for a fixed-channel controller. Captured wake publishers join before stop returns borrowed notification storage; a refused vector withdrawal retains the initialized owner for explicit retry. Each SoC wrapper verifies its actual SDK register offsets and bit definitions, supplies exact clock, DMA/IRQ and visible-memory facts, and binds the selected static state. Matching register names cannot establish another chip's routing, pin wiring, clock rate or errata policy."

msgid "The UART V1 channel-DMA engine is shared by the exact F103 and GD303 providers. Its wrappers assert legacy USART and fixed-channel DMA masks and layout. `dma-tx` owns one TX channel and an explicit IRQ byte ring; `dma-duplex` owns both channels and caller-provided finite RX blocks. Actual wire TC remains independent of DMA memory completion. The engine detaches each source, observes a stable remaining count and acknowledges flags before returning a buffer. Unprovable withdrawal retains the request or producer loan. Normal RX restarts through owner service, with explicit gaps and backpressure; no consumer block is overwritten. A byte discarded from DATA at a finite boundary records loss. Neither circular reception nor a cache contract is inferred from this engine."
msgstr "The UART V1 channel-DMA engine is shared by the exact F103 and GD303 providers. Its wrappers assert legacy USART and fixed-channel DMA masks and layout. `dma-tx` owns one TX channel and an explicit IRQ byte ring; `dma-duplex` owns both channels and caller-provided finite RX blocks. Actual wire TC remains independent of DMA memory completion. The engine detaches each source, observes a stable remaining count and acknowledges flags before returning a buffer. Unprovable withdrawal retains the request or producer loan. Normal RX restarts through owner service, with explicit gaps and backpressure; no consumer block is overwritten. A byte discarded from DATA at a finite boundary records loss. Neither circular reception nor a cache contract is inferred from this engine."

msgid "Keep per-byte operations shared only when their hardware protocol is identical. Cold validation, NVIC withdrawal and chip resources stay in SoC wrappers. A differing protocol or erratum requires a reviewed implementation or explicit narrow capability; do not add speculative family switches to a shared hot path. STM32 identity access remains in `soc/stm32/common/stm32_identity.h` and the cross-vendor SoC control contract remains in `soc/common/uart_control.h`."
msgstr "Keep per-byte operations shared only when their hardware protocol is identical. Cold validation, NVIC withdrawal and chip resources stay in SoC wrappers. A differing protocol or erratum requires a reviewed implementation or explicit narrow capability; do not add speculative family switches to a shared hot path. STM32 identity access remains in `soc/stm32/common/stm32_identity.h` and the cross-vendor SoC control contract remains in `soc/common/uart_control.h`."

msgid "CMake remains the only source graph. Unselected algorithms must not compile merely because their files exist here. Review the actual linked retention and resource costs of selected sources. Register-boundary models exercise the real engine and wrappers, including rejection, errors, cancel, failed drain and instance isolation. Compile each selected ARM implementation separately. Native models and linked ARM images establish different software properties; timing and electrical claims still require physical execution. See [execution budgets](/design/soc-execution-budgets.md) and the [provider guide](/guides/provider-porting.md)."
msgstr "CMake remains the only source graph. Unselected algorithms must not compile merely because their files exist here. Review the actual linked retention and resource costs of selected sources. Register-boundary models exercise the real engine and wrappers, including rejection, errors, cancel, failed drain and instance isolation. Compile each selected ARM implementation separately. Native models and linked ARM images establish different software properties; timing and electrical claims still require physical execution. See [execution budgets](/design/soc-execution-budgets.md) and the [provider guide](/guides/provider-porting.md)."
